// Editing with your fingers
// Tap the code to type. Above the
// keyboard, the symbol keys put
// " ( ) [ ] < > ~ * and more one tap
// away. Slide the row for the rest.
// A symbol key with text selected
// wraps it: ( makes (text).
//
// Try: put the cursor after hh and
// type *4 with the symbol keys, to
// get "bd sd hh*4". Then play.

$: s("bd sd hh")
// ---
// Moving the cursor
// The pencil at the left of the
// symbol keys opens the edit keys:
//  ‹ ›  one character: hold to
//       repeat, or slide on the key
//  « »  one word
//  { }  back to the symbol keys
//
// Try: put the cursor at the start
// of the last line, tap » until it
// is right after the first sd, and
// type :2 for another snare: sd:2

$: s("bd sd bd sd")
// ---
// Growing a selection
// Sel+ selects more at each tap: the
// word, the text in quotes, the
// quotes too, the whole call, the
// line, everything. Sel− goes back.
//
// Try: put the cursor in sawtooth,
// tap Sel+ and type square. Then put
// it in 400, tap Sel+ and type 1200.
// Update to hear both changes.

$: note("c2 c3")
  .s("sawtooth")
  .lpf(400)
// ---
// Line keys
// The ⋮ of the edit keys opens the
// line keys: duplicate, // comment,
// move up, move down, delete, undo.
//
// Try: put the cursor on the hh line
// and tap //: the line turns into a
// comment. Update: hh is gone. Tap
// // again to bring it back.
// Then duplicate a line, change the
// copy, and Update.

$: s("bd*2 sd")
$: s("hh*4")
// ---
// Muting a layer
// Put _ in front of $: and the layer
// goes quiet: _$: The hh layer below
// is muted that way.
//
// Try: delete the _ of the hh layer
// and Update. Then mute the cp layer
// with the _ of the symbol keys.

$: s("bd*2 sd")
$: s("~ cp")
_$: s("hh*4")
// ---
// Undo and a real keyboard
// Undo and redo are on the symbol
// keys, undo on the line keys too.
//
// With a hardware keyboard:
// Ctrl+Enter plays or updates,
// Ctrl+. stops, Ctrl+Z undoes.
//
// Try: change anything, then undo.
// Lesson 3 is about finding sounds
// and functions.

$: s("bd ~ sd bd")
